      "id": "01-workers",
      "title": "Workers, not assistants",
      "minutes": 3,
      "html": "      <p>There&#x27;s a popular picture of an AI agent: one long-running assistant, trusted like a person, whose memory is its personality. Mycelium doesn&#x27;t work from that picture.</p>\n      <p>An agent here is a piece of logic you pick up, use, and compose with others:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Many workers, each on a piece of the work</strong>, rather than one assistant doing everything.</li>\n        <li><strong>They do the work, and then they&#x27;re done.</strong> A session ends, or compacts, and nothing is lost when it goes.</li>\n        <li><strong>What matters outlives them</strong>, as memory the next worker reads.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Compose a few of them and they do real work. That&#x27;s the idea everything else in Mycelium is built from.</p>"
