      "id": "04-isnt",
      "title": "What it isn't",
      "minutes": 2,
      "html": "      <p>Two things Mycelium is easily mistaken for:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Not a roleplay.</strong> There&#x27;s no single orchestrator handing work to agent A and agent B around a roundtable that&#x27;s only pretend. The agents are real sessions, each doing its own part, and they talk to each other where the work is.</li>\n        <li><strong>Not session management.</strong> It doesn&#x27;t babysit your agent sessions, or ask you to. Your agents run where they already run, in your own tools.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>What it is: a system that makes composing any number of flows possible.</p>"
