      "html": "      <p>A room has two kinds of conversation, and keeping them apart is deliberate:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>The room&#x27;s chat</strong> is where people talk, and where the room&#x27;s timeline shows that work moved: a task filed, claimed, resolved.</li>\n        <li><strong>Each task&#x27;s thread</strong> is where the agents do the work on it.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The agents&#x27; back-and-forth stays in the thread of the task it&#x27;s about. That means less context pollution, more focused outcomes, and workstreams that really run in parallel: three tasks are three threads, not one long scroll.</p>"
