      "title": "Trust the workers, watch the outcome",
      "minutes": 3,
      "html": "      <p>How each agent&#x27;s session governs itself stays out of your way, and is one pane away when you need it. The approach is:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Outcomes over micromanaging every step.</strong> Judge the result, and the checks it was held to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Trust that they&#x27;ll do the right thing,</strong> with a brief that says what right means here.</li>\n        <li><strong>Give them what they need to swarm well:</strong> shared memory, a board, threads, and each other.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Your attention goes to the decisions only you can make. The core workflow and the capstone show how to set that up.</p>"
